    "cs_not_released_after_spi": {
      "mismatches": 0,
      "real_mismatches": 0,
      "detected": false,
      "equivalent_reason": "equivalent at the pins: when the S transaction ends the pins go back to qspi_reader, whose CS# is high (idle: CS# rises there, 8 cycles late) or low (burst parked by backpressure: CS# stays low with SCLK low and no clocks). The CS# rise that latches WREN/WRDI/WRR is only deferred to the next CS# rise, which always comes before any further command byte is clocked: the next S frame forces CS# high first (S_PT_WAIT sets cs_n_q=1 before pt_active) and a decode seek raises it in qspi_reader. WEL/WIP are only observed through S frames or take effect before the next decode read, so the deferral is unobservable; the directed WREN/RDSR/WRDI/RDSR cases between decode steps (reader parked with CS# low) pass with the fault",
      "ok": true
    },
