    "spi_takeover_without_settle_wait": {
      "mismatches": 0,
      "real_mismatches": 0,
      "detected": false,
      "equivalent_reason": "equivalent: the 256-cycle wait only guards against taking the pins while the reader still clocks its last prefetched byte. The reader parks within about 16 cycles of the last byte top_decode accepts, which is before done; the host cannot send an S frame before it has received the 11-byte R response (11 x 10 bit times >= 880 cycles at 115200 baud, 880 cycles even at CPB=8 x 10 x 11) and the S header itself takes 3 more byte times, so the wait is always already elapsed in a protocol-conforming exchange. Removing it is unobservable",
      "ok": true
    }
